# Weights. These live on HuggingFace (owner: owenmorgan) and are pulled on
# first run with sha256 verification. A multi-gigabyte GGUF has no business in
# git, and a weight file in a diff is a sign something resolved to the wrong
# directory.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
# ANCHORED, deliberately. An unanchored `models/` also matches `src/models/`,
# which is the catalog/download/paths CODE — git silently refused to stage it.
/models/

# Vendored binaries: the pinned tesseract + tessdata and the bundled
# llama-server. Fetched by the packaging step, never committed.
#
# The PIN, though, is code. vendor/tesseract/manifest.json records the expected
# version and the tessdata sha256s and src/scan/tesseract.ts verifies against it
# before reading a page, so it and its README are re-included. Directory-first:
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so
# `!/vendor/tesseract/` has to come before the files inside it.
/vendor/**
!/vendor/tesseract/
!/vendor/tesseract/manifest.json
!/vendor/tesseract/README.md

node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Bun. The lockfile is NOT ignored — this ships as a binary, so the dependency
# set has to be reproducible.
.bun/

# Scratch
*.log
tmp/
.cache/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
